{"crc":"dfd5c9e8","kind":"Candidate","payload":{"response":"Looking at this issue, the problem is in the `FigureCanvasMac.resize` method in `backend_macosx.py`. When a figure is unpickled, the `resize` method is called, and it's dividing by `self.device_pixel_ratio` which causes the DPI to be doubled on M1 Macs.\n\nThe issue is that `device_pixel_ratio` is not properly initialized when the canvas is created during unpickling. The fix should ensure that `device_pixel_ratio` is properly set to 1.0 when the canvas is initialized.\n\nHere's the fix:\n\n# path: lib/matplotlib/backends/backend_macosx.py\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n    def __init__(self, figure):\n        super().__init__(figure=figure)\n        self._draw_pending = False\n        self._is_drawing = False\n=======\n    def __init__(self, figure):\n        super().__init__(figure=figure)\n        self._draw_pending = False\n        self._is_drawing = False\n        self.device_pixel_ratio = 1.0\n>>>>>>> REPLACE","round":1,"slot":0},"producer":{"instance":"01KZQE67RM38XB8EEJS0XHHPX0","kind":"drafter","parent":"01KZQE67RGCB5YDNB03C49CHCC"},"schema":"Candidate@1","seq":20,"t":1786419292.108004}
